        { id: "s17", label: "17. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Recognising the future tax consequences of today's temporary differences</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 18 governs the RECOGNITION and MEASUREMENT of CURRENT and DEFERRED income TAX — REQUIRING enterprises to RECOGNISE deferred TAX assets and LIABILITIES for the FUTURE tax CONSEQUENCES of TEMPORARY differences BETWEEN the ACCOUNTING carrying AMOUNT of assets/LIABILITIES and their TAX bases. This STANDARD represented a GENUINELY significant MODERNISATION when it was FIRST introduced (Section 2).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>A Landmark 2006 Reform — Introducing the Balance Sheet Liability Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Replacing the older tax payable and deferral methods</div><div class="principle">PRIOR to the 2006 ASBE OVERHAUL, Chinese ENTERPRISES could APPLY various OLDER approaches to INCOME tax accounting — INCLUDING the "TAX PAYABLE method" (WHICH recognised NO deferred tax AT ALL, simply EXPENSING the CURRENT period's TAX payable) and an OLDER "DEFERRAL method." The 2006 REFORM INTRODUCED the "BALANCE SHEET LIABILITY method" for the FIRST time — a GENUINELY significant MODERNISATION, bringing CHINA'S income tax ACCOUNTING into LINE with IAS 12's OWN internationally-established APPROACH.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">All enterprises subject to income tax</div><div class="text-supporting">This Standard applies to ALL enterprises SUBJECT to Chinese CORPORATE income TAX, ADDRESSING both the CURRENT period's tax PAYABLE and the FUTURE tax CONSEQUENCES arising FROM temporary DIFFERENCES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Temporary Differences — Comparing Carrying Amount to Tax Base</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Item-by-item comparison, generating deferred tax</div><div class="text-supporting">DEFERRED tax is DETERMINED by COMPARING the ACCOUNTING carrying AMOUNT of EACH asset and LIABILITY to its TAX BASIS — TEMPORARY differences (e.g. a PROVISION recognised for ACCOUNTING purposes but NOT yet tax-DEDUCTIBLE) give RISE to a DEFERRED tax ASSET or LIABILITY, REFLECTING the FUTURE tax CONSEQUENCE when the DIFFERENCE eventually REVERSES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Deferred Tax Asset Recognition — the "Probable" Threshold</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A general, judgement-based test — not a structured classification framework</div><div class="text-supporting">A DEFERRED tax ASSET is RECOGNISED to the EXTENT it is PROBABLE that SUFFICIENT future TAXABLE profit will be AVAILABLE against WHICH the TEMPORARY difference (or TAX loss carryforward) can be UTILISED — a GENERAL, PRINCIPLES-based "PROBABLE" threshold, CONSISTENT with IAS 12's OWN approach. This CONTRASTS with the MORE structured, TIERED "company CLASSIFICATION" recoverability FRAMEWORK applied UNDER Japan GAAP (see the COMPANION ASBJ Statement No. 28 poster EARLIER in this SERIES) — ASBE'S approach is MORE judgement-DRIVEN, RATHER than FORMULA-based.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Recognition Exceptions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Narrow carve-outs from general deferred tax recognition</div><div class="text-supporting">A DEFERRED tax LIABILITY is NOT recognised for the INITIAL recognition of GOODWILL, or for the INITIAL recognition of an ASSET or LIABILITY in a TRANSACTION that is NOT a BUSINESS combination and AFFECTS neither ACCOUNTING profit NOR taxable PROFIT at the TIME of the transaction — NARROW, TECHNICAL exceptions CONSISTENT with IAS 12's OWN equivalent carve-OUTS internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Measurement — Enacted or Substantively Enacted Tax Rates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Using the rate expected to apply on reversal</div><div class="text-supporting">DEFERRED tax ASSETS and LIABILITIES are MEASURED using TAX rates that are ENACTED (or SUBSTANTIVELY enacted) as of the REPORTING date, and EXPECTED to APPLY in the PERIOD the TEMPORARY difference is EXPECTED to REVERSE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>No Discounting</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Deferred tax balances are not present-valued</div><div class="text-supporting">DEFERRED tax ASSETS and LIABILITIES are NOT discounted to PRESENT value, REGARDLESS of HOW far in the FUTURE the UNDERLYING temporary DIFFERENCE is EXPECTED to REVERSE — CONSISTENT with IAS 12's OWN no-discounting RULE internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>China's Standard Tax Rate and Preferential Regimes</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A standard rate, with meaningful preferential variations</div><div class="text-supporting">CHINA'S STANDARD corporate INCOME tax rate is 25%, though NUMEROUS preferential RATES apply in PRACTICE — INCLUDING a REDUCED 15% rate for QUALIFYING high-TECHNOLOGY enterprises, and VARIOUS reduced RATES for SMALL and MICRO enterprises MEETING specified CRITERIA. THESE preferential RATES materially AFFECT the MEASUREMENT of BOTH current and DEFERRED tax for QUALIFYING enterprises.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — Recognising a Deferred Tax Liability</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A taxable temporary difference from accelerated tax depreciation</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Faster tax depreciation than accounting depreciation</div><div class="wk-body">A company's equipment has an accounting carrying amount of RMB 80,000,000, but a tax base of RMB 60,000,000 (reflecting faster depreciation allowed for tax purposes). The applicable tax rate is 25%.</div><div class="wk-answer">The TAXABLE temporary DIFFERENCE of RMB 80,000,000 − RMB 60,000,000 = RMB 20,000,000 GIVES rise to a DEFERRED tax LIABILITY of RMB 20,000,000 × 25% = <strong>RMB 5,000,000</strong>.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Worked Example — Recognising a Deferred Tax Asset</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A deductible temporary difference from a provision</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A warranty provision not yet tax-deductible</div><div class="wk-body">A company recognises a warranty provision of RMB 8,000,000 (see the companion ASBE No. 13 poster), which is not tax-deductible until the warranty costs are actually paid. The company expects sufficient future taxable profit, and the tax rate is 25%.</div><div class="wk-answer">The DEDUCTIBLE temporary DIFFERENCE of RMB 8,000,000 GIVES rise to a DEFERRED tax ASSET of RMB 8,000,000 × 25% = <strong>RMB 2,000,000</strong>, since SUFFICIENT future TAXABLE profit is CONSIDERED probable.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 18 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Components of deferred tax assets and liabilities, by type of temporary difference</span><span>Reconciliation between accounting profit and taxable profit (or the effective tax rate)</span><span>Unrecognised deductible temporary differences and tax loss carryforwards</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether it is probable that sufficient future taxable profit will support recognition of a deferred tax asset</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Projected future taxable income supporting deferred tax asset recognition</span><span>Timing of reversal for temporary differences</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 12</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 18 vs IAS 12</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 18</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 12</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Overall approach</span><span>Balance sheet liability method</span><span>Balance sheet liability method — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>DTA recognition threshold</span><span>Probable (general judgement)</span><span>Probable (general judgement) — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard — THIS represents ONE of the CLEAREST examples of the 2006 REFORM successfully MODERNISING a PREVIOUSLY outdated Chinese accounting AREA into ALIGNMENT with INTERNATIONAL practice.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every income tax event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Deferred tax asset/liability</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised for temporary differences, subject to the probable threshold for assets</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 20</span><span>Business Combinations — the initial goodwill recognition exception this Standard carves out</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s17"><span class="num">17</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Balance sheet liability method</div><div class="glossary-def">A method comparing the accounting carrying amount of assets and liabilities to their tax bases, recognising deferred tax for the resulting temporary differences.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Tax base</div><div class="glossary-def">The amount attributed to an asset or liability for tax purposes, compared against its accounting carrying amount to determine temporary differences.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe18 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
